iniquity no knowledge,","poem":1},{"text":"who eat up my people as they eat bread,","poem":2},{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"and don’t call on God?","poem":2}]},{"type":"verse","number":5,"content":[{"text":"There they were in great fear, where no fear was,","poem":1},{"text":"for God has scattered the bones of him who encamps against you.","poem":2},{"text":"You have put them to shame,","poem":1},{"text":"because God has rejected them.","poem":2}]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":[{"text":"Oh that the yishu'ah ·salvation· of Israel [God prevails] would come out of Zion [Mountain ridge, Marking]!","poem":1},{"text":"When God brings back his people from captivity,","poem":2},{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"then Jacob [Supplanter] shall rejoice,","poem":2},{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"and Israel [God prevails] shall be glad.","poem":2}]},{"type":"line_break"}],"footnotes":[{"noteId":121,"caller":"+","text":". (1-3) Quoted in  Rom 3:10-12","reference":{"chapter":53,"verse":3}}]},"thisChapterLink":"/api/eng_our/PSA/53.json","thisChapterAudioLinks":{},"nextChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_our/PSA/54.json","nextChapterAudioLinks":{},"previousChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_our/PSA/52.json","previousChapterAudioLinks":{},"numberOfVerses":6}